# =============================================================================
# .gitignore -- WH_BOR_Trout
#
# PRINCIPLE: commit CODE and DOCUMENTATION. Never commit DATA or OUTPUT.
#
# The test for whether a file belongs in the repository:
#   "If I deleted this, could I regenerate it by re-running the pipeline?"
#   Yes -> ignore it.  No -> commit it.
#
# *** THIS FILE ONLY STOPS UNTRACKED FILES FROM BEING ADDED. ***
# It does NOT untrack a file that was already committed. A blob committed once
# stays in the history permanently, and `git push` sends the history -- which is
# how 800 MB of model output (beta_recruitment.rds 368 MB, beta_survival.rds
# 354 MB, response.rds 78 MB) came to be rejected by GitHub's 100 MB limit long
# after the files had been deleted from the working tree.
#
# If that happens, see docs/GITHUB_PAGES.md -> "Large files rejected".
# To untrack something already committed:  git rm -r --cached <path>
# =============================================================================


# --- R and RStudio -----------------------------------------------------------
.Rhistory
.Rapp.history
.RData
.Ruserdata
.Rproj.user/
.Renviron


# --- DATA --------------------------------------------------------------------
# Referenced through CFG$paths, never copied into the project. Some of it is
# large and some may carry access restrictions from Montana FWP.
data/
Data/
imputed_output/


# --- MODEL OUTPUT ------------------------------------------------------------
# output/ holds everything the pipeline produces: .rds objects passed between
# scripts, result tables, and figures. All regenerable by RUN_ALL.R.
#
# The .rds files here are the ones that broke the repository. beta_*.rds carry
# 365 columns x thousands of posterior draws and reach hundreds of megabytes.
output/
Output/


# --- broad data-format rules -------------------------------------------------
# Deliberately broad: these formats are output or input in this project, never
# source. Anything that must be committed needs an explicit exception at the
# foot of this file, added consciously.
*.rds
*.RDS
*.RData
*.csv
*.xlsx
*.xls


# --- RENDERED WEBSITE --------------------------------------------------------
# render_site.R builds _site/ and publish_site.sh pushes it to the gh-pages
# branch as a single orphan commit. It must NOT be committed to main: that is
# what made gh-pages inherit main's history in the first place.
#
# manuscript/figures/ is a staging copy render_site.R makes so the pages can
# reference figures relatively. The published copies travel inside _site/.
_site/
manuscript/figures/
manuscript/*_files/


# --- GENERATED PAGES ---------------------------------------------------------
# render_site.R writes one wrapper per active site plus the hub, from
# manuscript/_site_template.Rmd. Build products: edit the template, never these.
# Regenerated on every render, so a removed site cannot linger as a page.
manuscript/site_*.Rmd
manuscript/results.Rmd


# --- knitr / rmarkdown intermediates ------------------------------------------
*.html
*_files/
*_cache/
*.knit.md
*.utf8.md


# --- git worktree used by publish_site.sh -------------------------------------
# Normally removed by the cleanup trap. Ignored so that an interrupted run
# cannot leave a second full checkout of the site to be swept up by `git add -A`.
.gh-pages-worktree/


# --- OS noise ----------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini


# =============================================================================
# EXCEPTIONS
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Nothing data-shaped is excepted. In particular:
#
#   * The standardization constants live inside output/models/flow.rds and are
#     regenerated by R/02_build_flow.R. An earlier version of this file kept an
#     exception for data/flow_fd/*_climatology.rds; that path belonged to the
#     previous pipeline and no longer exists.
#
#   * config_local.R is NOT ignored, and must not be. It holds the site
#     registry, the per-site flow lags, and the analysis choices -- part of the
#     analysis, and not regenerable. It is the one settings file that is yours
#     rather than shipped.
#
# `git add -f <file>` forces a one-off without editing this file.
# =============================================================================
!.gitignore
!*.Rproj